// Synced from cheneygross-afk/lengo:src/lib/lessons/lessonVideos.ts by scripts/sync-content.mjs -- edit it there, not here.
// Real, official videos LINKED from the course -- never embedded, downloaded,
// transcribed or re-hosted. Each entry is a title, a YouTube videoId (opened
// on youtube.com via videoUrlFor) and the channel that owns it in `source`
// ("Channel · Series/Level"). Only uploads from the channel that made the
// video, no third-party re-uploads or compilations. Each video appears once.
//
// Sources, roughly by level:
// - Dreaming Spanish (youtube.com/@DreamingSpanish): Superbeginner /
//   Beginner / Intermediate / Advanced playlists, plus its older Books and
//   TV Shows series.
// - Easy Spanish (youtube.com/@EasySpanish): Super Easy Spanish (slow,
//   subtitled beginner dialogues and city tours, A1-A2), the numbered street
//   interviews in Mexico City and Barcelona (B1-B2) and the Easy Spanish
//   Podcast (B2-C1).
// - Butterfly Spanish (beginner explanations), Spanish After Hours
//   (comprehensible-input vlogs and podcasts) and Español con Juan (Spain,
//   B2-C1 talks for learners).
// - Duolingo Spanish Podcast (youtube.com/@duolingo), B2.
// - BBC News Mundo (youtube.com/@BBCMundo): native explainers about the
//   Spanish language (C1) and science and history (C2).
//
// Two lists:
// - LESSON_VIDEOS: shown after one lesson ("Now watch this video"), only
//   where the video's topic plausibly matches the lesson -- a daily-routine
//   vlog after the reflexive-verbs lesson, a muy/mucho explainer after the
//   muy/mucho lesson, Rioplatense pronunciation after a voseo drill. Keyed by
//   the lesson's level and exact slug; `npm run check-content` fails if a
//   slug stops matching a lesson.
// - LEVEL_WATCH_VIDEOS: general listening videos at each level, listed on
//   the level page and grouped by `topic`.
// The pick leaves out videos built around provocative or dating-gossip
// premises and channel promotion.
